{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-350322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3})]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-6(0-\\frac{1}{27}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b"} {"question" "q-350322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{x}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{2}{7}{x}^{-7/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{a}^{7}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{7}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152777" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfb