ng the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{(2x+4)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-2{u}^{-1/2}]}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}]}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}}] \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b"} {"question" "q-152045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-152045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{2}+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-2{u}^{-1/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc7249993406af5b"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-118618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u={x}^{4}+2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{4}+2$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{4}+2)^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}{u}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-2{u}^{-1/2}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-1/2}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{1/2}}-\\frac{1}{{2}^{1/2}}] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a3d73c51146b85d3c689cbb12e17c81e754ed69e12ac978d6e26e0f09761645"} {"question" "q-350534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007645/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4a0113cdf61e3bfbe63d30e1064ed1367e3e933afe27bca9cc72499